  "question": {
    "text": "Electric field in a certain region is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>. The SI unit of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are :",
    "image": null
  },
